{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026053438c9249cc002bd416d","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze this task. I need to research the Roman aqueduct of Naissus (Niš, Serbia) and the water supply of the Mediana villa. I have four questions:\n\n1. Literature about the aqueduct/water supply of Naissus and Mediana: published route? Who claims water comes from Oblik hill, who from Niška Banja thermal springs? Key authors: Mihailo Jeremić (Starinar 39/1988), Petar Petrović, Slobodan Pop-Lazić, \"Constantine's Villa at Mediana\" monograph.\n2. Geography: Oblik hill — coordinates and elevation; Niška Banja springs — elevation, water temperature, capacity l/s. Is gravity flow possible to Mediana (198 m asl)?\n3. Roman aqueduct routes in Dardania/Moesia for comparison: Ulpiana, Skupi, Viminacium, Singidunum, Gamzigrad (Romuliana) — published routes and lengths?\n4. Any archaeological finds of aqueduct channel between Oblik/Niška Banja and Mediana (excavations, geomagnetic prospection, aerial photos)?\n\nI should return raw data: URL, exact quote or paraphrase with numbers, confidence rating. Write in Serbian Latin script. Max info density.\n\nLet me start with parallel web searches.","signature":"b9b671d5e31f440e9ac769b4"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_e7c41a7c411c422ea065942e","session_id":"1ba7b4f2-4571-4068-8385-8222f6e774c0","uuid":"45f95d0c-9a0d-429c-a57d-b9408a43a2ef","timestamp":"2026-10-25T21:34:45.947Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Istraži akvadukt Naissusa"}
