nt: Aqua Augusta 34 km, drop 12 m? Actually Serino aqueduct: average gradient ~ 0.4%? Nîmes: 50 km, total drop 12.6 m → 0.025%. Mediana 2% is 60-80x steeper — flag as either (a) trasa much longer than 500 m (if source at Niška Banja, ~10-15 km away, gradient could be gentle), or (b) the channel used stepped drops/cascades, or (c) castellum estimate 206 is wrong.\n\nActually this is a good argument for the source conflict: if the source is Niška Banja (~10 km away, altitude ~250-300 m at the spring — Niška Banja thermal springs emerge at ~250 m? Let me check: Niška Banja lies at ~250 m elevation; springs (Suva Banja, main spring \"Glavno vrelo\" ~ 15-17 °C) at approx 250 m). Naissus/Mediana at 198-206 m. Over ~12 km, drop from 250 to 206 = 44 m → average gradient 0.37% — very Roman. That supports the Niška Banja hypothesis hydraulically for a long line. For Oblik: hill Oblik — where is it? There's \"Oblik\" hill near Niš? Let me research. Some sources say the water was brought from the spring on the Oblik hill (Suva Planina?) Actually \"Oblik\" might be a spring on the slopes near Niška Banja — Oblik is a peak of Suva Planina? Hmm: Suva planina has peaks Trem (1810), Mosor, etc. There's \"Oblik\" above Niška Banja? I recall the village \"Oblik\" near Prokuplje? There's also \"Oblik\" hill in the Toplica region. Need web search.\n\nAlso relevant literature: \"Akvedukt antičkog Naissusa\" — there might be a paper by M. Korkut? Or \"Water supply of Naissus\" by Gordana Jeremić? Known: Jeremić G., \"Castellum aquae antičke Medijane\", Starinar 39 (1988). Also possibly \"Vodovod antičkog Naissa\" by ...? Let me search web.\n\n4. **Odluci i odvodnja vile** — drainage: Mediana terme, horreum pools 1.40 m (cella vinaria), the \"kanali za odvod\". Literature: monografija mentions \"mreža vodovodnih i odvodnih kanala\" (v0.9, from the monografija: \"druga faza: ... impluvium, mreža vodovodnih i odvodnih kanala\"). So there's an impluvium — good. Cite monografija handle 1539 UR