{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261026060010090e2252ce3f4c14","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Str065.png = printed page 62 of Starinar 39 (1988), Miroslav Jeremić, \"Castellum aquae antičke Medijane\". Key content:\n\n- **Položaj kasteluma**: Medijana ~4,5 km istočno od Niša, selo Brzi Brod; naselje ~40 ha; left bank of Nišava to fabrički kompleks Elektronske industrije; at the foot of Vlaškog brda (can't fully read but consistent). Trasa savremenog puta Niš—Pretor/ Niš—Pirot? It says \"trasom savremenog puta Niš—Pirot\"? Actually it says \"Niš—Пирот\" (Pirot). OK.\n- The complex: monumental object of rectangular osnova with bazen u atrijumu, peristil with mosaics, many thysuses (tisin prostorija?) and polupodzemnim nimfejum on northern side (сл. 1). Called palata.\n- In vicinity: hotteum (horeum?) ~130 m zapadno od palate; two villa rustica objects, cut by modern road Niš—Pirot; large object ~170 m severoistočno od palate, which Kanić called baptisterijum.\n- Footnote 4: Petrović, Niš u antičko doba, 69; medijanska nekropola južno od puta.\n- 1971 excavations južna strana puta — sonde bez očekivanih rezultata.\n\nSo the article's fig. 1 is the situational plan (on page ~65/66?). The article starts around printed page 59-61 (proba_p058/060/062 probably cover the beginning: introduction, položaj). Let me now read str066-str087 in order — the meat: description of the kula, two basins, dimensions, dating, source of water, channels, conclusion.\n\nI'll read them in batches of 4. Take careful notes. This is the core primary source — worth the context.","signature":"60d1464e04954e21a8cf32ec"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1438346-843d-4d42-b992-1d35828f0fa4","uuid":"0c49d63f-787f-4ea1-9755-fa4215e4ab10","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:00:24.690Z"}
