oupe refers to the terrain slope of the gully stretch. For the aqueduct: if it hugs contours around the spur rather than dropping into the valley, the line length is longer and effective gradient lower. I'll compute both scenarios.\n\nLet me continue reading: str067, 068, 069... The description of the kula with two basins, dimensions, and — crucially — any statement about the water source. Let me read the next pages.","signature":"fbe8b04c3a1a447cac96c968"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1438346-843d-4d42-b992-1d35828f0fa4","uuid":"bea1a959-d77c-4fc0-a1eb-72e2d73f9e75","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:00:55.820Z"}
