{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606034009d35d9afc394cd4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"STR071 = printed page 68 — photos Sl. 6-7 + **Sl. 8: Poprečni presek c—c kroz bazen A (prostor e)** with legend:\n\n1. ružičasti malter (mortier rougeâtre — pink/reddish mortar = opus signinum!)\n2. sloj kaličinacije(? \"калcинaциje\" = calcaire deposit — \"dépôt de calcaire\" = LIME DEPOSIT/ Scale!) — **sloj kalcinacije = krečni talog (_incrustrations_)** — proof water ran through with mineral scale\n3. zaštitna konstrukcija (construction protectrice)\n4. **olovna drenažna cev G — Ø 155 mm (tuyau d'évacuation plomb G — Ø 155 mm)** — CONFIRMED 155 mm\n5. platforma od opeke (plate-forme en brique)\n6. **kanal E (conduit E)**\n7. sloj žute peskulje (couche d'argile sableux)\n\nKote on the section: 207.4 (top left, wall of A), 205.98 (floor of A in section?), 205.88 (at the G pipe), 205.98(?) right, 205.49(?), 205.61 at the right wall (top of wall 6 near kanal E?). Section shows: basin A wall (dark hatched left), floor with layers (1,2 = mortar + lime scale), the arched channel with G pipe (Ø155) running at 205.88, bricks platform, then to the right the wall and kanal E below (7 = yellow sandy clay below).\n\nWait, actually looking again: the arched structure in the middle with the black circle = the G pipe in an arched channel under the floor of basin A/B junction; kota 205.88 next to it. The \"platforma od opeke\" (5) — brick platform. Kanal E (6) — at right side.\n\nHmm — actually legend order and drawing positions: 1 → pink mortar on wall (left), 2 → lime scale layer on floor, 3 → protective construction (arch over pipe), 4 → the G pipe itself, 5 → brick platform under the pipe, 6 → kanal E (the opening at right), 7 → yellow sandy clay layer (natural).\n\nThe section c—c through basin A (space e — the narrow northern part). Kote: 207.4 = preserved wall crown on left (outer edge); 205.98 = floor level of A at this section; G pipe at 205.88 (its channel under the floor); 205.61 at the right wall — kanal E top?\n\nSo now the vertical model of castellum:\n- Wall crown preserved ~207.4 (in space e)\n- Floor of basin A (north part e) ~205.98\n- G drain pipe axis ~205.88\n- Basin B floor ~205.5–205.6 (from Sl. 2 readings: 205.5, 205.6)\n- Kanal E exit ~205.3–205.6\n- 1.08 m fall of A's bottom from south (a, ~207.0?) to north (e, ~205.98): 207.06 - 205.98 = 1.08 → south end of A floor ~207.06.\n\nAlso \"sloj kalcinacije\" — lime scale — direct physical evidence that water flowed through and was hard water (karst spring → supports Niška Banja thermal/karst springs!). Scale deposits also prove the basins actually held water.\n\nPhotos: Sl. 6 — drain pipe G in basin A (visible round lead pipe end); Sl. 7 — connection of basins A and B.\n\nNext: str072 (printed 69) — BAZEN B text.","signature":"e2d28d64899a41c8a1a06d06"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1438346-843d-4d42-b992-1d35828f0fa4","uuid":"9423e34e-ed71-4f4d-a1b5-b084fcefb461","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:04:03.571Z"}
