{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026102606053629b473f53d12426f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3-flash","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"STR075 = printed page 72 — CRITICAL HYDRAULIC DATA on kanal C:\n\n- Kanal C: priključak u bazen A uništen u srednjem delu; **širina ~60 cm** (\"Širina mu je 60 cm, koliko približno iznosi i njegova najveća zabeležena očuvana visina\"). Širina zidova varira 50–100 cm zapadno, 60 cm istočno. Zidani od lomljenog kamena i oblutaka u krečnom malteru. **Dno kanala od vodootpornog ružičastog maltera** (istog kao u bazenima) preko podloge od sitnog lomljenog kamena i frgamenata opeke u krečnom malteru. Unutrašnje površine omalterisane istim vodootpornim malterom debljine 2 cm, sa pomenutim podom čine monolitnu celinu. Uobičajena zadebljanja („lajsne\") u uglovima bočnih zidova sa podom.\n- **Dno kanala C nije jednoteran(?) — nije jednometan(?)**: \"pod dužnom presjek pod očuvane deonice kanala, dno se očituje kao konkavna linija (сл. 18). **Najviša zabeležena kota na istočnom kraju kanala iznosi 209,50 m, odakle se pod promenljivim nagibom od 2 do 13‰ spušta do najniže tačke na koti od 208,92 m, koja se nalazi približno u podužnoj osnovini kasteluma, da bi zatim nastavio ka zapadu sa usponom od 2,7‰. Najviša zabeležena kota na zapadnom kraju očuvane deonice iznosi 209,16 m, što u odnosu na niveletu dna kanala na njegovom istočnom kraju daje visinsku razliku od 34 cm (сл. 2 и 18).**\"\n\n  WOW — the channel C bottom is CONCAVE: from east end 209.50 falling at 2–13‰ to 208.92 (at castellum axis), then RISING westward at 2.7‰ to 209.16. This is a classic ** settling/collection feature**: the channel dips at the castellum — like a sediment trap / last settling stretch before the basins. Height difference 34 cm. Interesting: so the incoming water at the castellum is at ~208.9-209.2.\n\n  Wait — \"uspon od 2,7‰\" — the bottom RISES toward the west (toward the basins?)? That's hydraulically weird for supply... unless the channel continues west past the castellum as an overflow/waste channel, or the concave dip is a settling basin in the channel. Actually re-read: \"spušta do najniže tačke na koti od 208,92 m, koja se nalazi približno u podužnoj osnovini kasteluma, da bi zatim nastavio ka zapadu sa usponom od 2,7‰\" — so the dip lowest point 208.92 at castellum axis, then rises westward to 209.16. If kanal C feeds the castellum AT its axis (priključak u bazen A), then east of that point the channel descends toward the inlet (correct: water flows down into the castellum), and WEST of the inlet the channel continues and RISES — that western part can't carry water to anywhere higher... unless it's a **redundant/revision channel** (the \"revizioni kanal\" from Pop-Lazić!) or an overflow spillway. Hmm. Or the western part is where the channel continues to a second inlet. The base vodeni sloj says: \"Iz kule vodotornja na severnom delu objekta voda se sprovodi glavnim kanalom i jednim revizionim (rezervnim) kanalom prema naselju\" (Pop-Lazić) — those are OUTPUT channels E + another. The C-channel west rise: maybe just the excavated stretch that wasn't fully understood. I'll note the concavity + kote as measured, interpretation flagged.\n\n  Hmm, actually alternative reading: maybe kanal C's dip is because the survey line follows the channel as excavated (33 m), and the \"uspon ka zapadu\" is west of the castellum axis toward... the western part of the complex (H structure?). Enough — record data.\n\n- **\"U zapadnom delu kanala C, nasuprot jugozapadnom uglu kasteluma, otkriven je in situ, u ravni dna kanala, pravilan kameni blok dimenzija: 90×64×15 cm (сл. 16 и 19). Na njegovoj gornjoj površini uklesan je žljeb dimenzija 58×6×5 cm, koji stoji upravno u odnosu na pravac pružanja kanala. Ovaj žljeb predstavlja ležište ustave (na planu ustava I, сл. 2). Jednim povremenim podizanjem i spuštanjem, regulisano je napajanje kasteluma vodom.¹⁵\"**\n\n  **USTAVA (sluice gate/gate valve!)**: stone block 90×64×15 cm with groove 58×6×5 cm perpendicular to channel — seat of a sluice gate; raising/lowering regulated the supply! Footnote 15: \"Peti slučaj kamenih ležišta ustava, dimenzija sličnih našem primeru, zabeležio je B. Ilakovac na trasi akvedukta Boljkovac — Nin(?). B. Ilakovac, Rimski akvedukti na području severne Dalmacije, Zagreb 1982, 115–120.\" — FIFTH case of stone gate seats; comparanda from Dalmatian aqueducts (Burnum/Boljkovac aqueduct near Knin).\n\n  This is a beautiful detail for the 3D model: an operating sluice gate (ustava) on the inflow channel.\n\n- Sl. 14: bazen B sa početkom olovne drenažne cevi kanala F; Sl. 15: **kalcinacija na severnom zidu bazena B** (\"Les traces de calcination\" = actually calcaire — lime scale traces).\n\nNext page str076 (printed 73): kanal D, kanal E details, then probably chronology + hydrology calculations. Continue.","signature":"c0a49645896248a6b97da193"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1438346-843d-4d42-b992-1d35828f0fa4","uuid":"82f9056c-9b80-45b5-bb71-246c0c70d599","timestamp":"2026-10-25T22:06:13.354Z"}
